in the Italian music, a sort of sacred drama of dialogues; containing recitatives, duetos, trios, ritornellos, choruses, &c. The subjects of those pieces are usually taken from scripture, <a class="xref" href="vol8.html#article-OR">or</a> the <a class="xref" href="vol0.html#article-LIFE">life</a> of some saint, &c. The music for the oratorios should be in the finest <a class="xref" href="vol10.html#article-TASTE">taste</a> and best chosen strains. These oratorios are greatly used at Rome in the <a class="xref" href="vol0.html#article-TIME">time</a> of <a class="xref" href="vol6.html#article-LENT">Lent</a>, and of late in England.
ORATORY;
The art of speaking well upon any subject, in order to persuade.
